    "result_text": "Each project now has a task list. You can add tasks and tick them off, or reopen them, from the project's page. The acceptance test passes under `bin/e2e`.\n\nOne mismatch with the request: it asked for an \"OfficeFloor server\", but this app is a Spring Boot app (only the Java package is named `net.officefloor`), and CLAUDE.md says to follow Spring conventions. I built the server side in Spring, copying how contacts and invoices are done.\n\n**Database:** `V9__create_task.sql` adds a `task` table holding the project it belongs to, a title, and a done flag that starts as false.\n\n**Server** (new code in `.../app/task/`):\n- Three endpoints under `/api/projects/{projectId}/tasks`: list a project's tasks, add one, and toggle one between open and done.\n- Each toggle writes an audit line like `TASK_TOGGLED id=1 done=true`, which is what the test checks for.\n- The test-only reset and seed endpoints now clear the task table and accept a `tasks` list in the test data.\n\n**Front end:**\n- A new task section on the project page, placed above the invoices.\n- It has a form to add a task and a table showing each task's title, its status (OPEN or DONE) and a button to tick it off or reopen it.\n- The test IDs match the spec: `project-tasks-table`, `task-row-{id}`, `task-title`, `task-status` and `task-toggle-{id}`.\n\nThe add-task form isn't covered by the spec, so it hasn't been tested.",
